build/
build-*/
*.mlir.prj/
*.o
*.log
compile_commands.json
.cache/
__pycache__/

# Mesh runtime state (runs, leases, sessions, artifacts) - never commit
.pi/mesh/

# ctest run in the source tree (kept out of the PR by the copyright check)
Testing/

# the HRX toolchain the build fetches (scripts/fetch-rocm-sdk.sh, config/hrx-toolchain.config):
# a multi-gigabyte venv of TheRock's ROCm SDK at the pinned version, not part of the source
third_party/toolchain/

# the model-pin sweep writes these where it runs (tools/pin_watch.py --check --json)
pin-report.md
pin-report.json

# HRX probe run output: the .hrx123 probe tools write JSONL logs here. Run output is not source and carries no
# licence notice, but tools/copyright.py deliberately also checks untracked-but-not-ignored files (so a new file
# is caught before `git add`), so leaving these unignored reds the gate on every developer clone that has run a
# probe - a red that is the tree's, not the repository's (engine#1564). Ignoring them also stops run output being
# committed by accident.
.hrx123/logs/
